hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2788","**\nNarrated to us Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la, who said: Ibn Wahb informed us, on the authority of Malik, who said: Ibn Shihab informed him, on the authority of 'Urwah, on the authority of 'A'ishah (RA), who said:\n\"We set out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for the Farewell Pilgrimage, and we entered the state of ihram for 'umrah.\"\nShe added: \"I arrived in Makkah while I was menstruating. I had not performed tawaf around the House, nor the sa'i between Safa and Marwah. I complained about this to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he said: 'Untie your hair, comb it, and enter the state of ihram for Hajj, leaving the 'umrah.'\"\nShe said: \"So I did that. When we had completed the Hajj, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me with 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr to al-Tan'im, where I performed 'umrah.\"\nHe (the narrator) said: \"This is the place for your 'umrah.\"\n\nAbu Bakr (the narrator) said: \"For a long time, I had doubts about the wording in the report of 'A'ishah (RA), particularly the statement of the Prophet (ﷺ) to her: 'Untie your hair and comb it.' I feared that it might imply that the Prophet (ﷺ) had commanded her to abandon the 'umrah entirely. However, I later found evidence supporting our view.\"\n\nHe added: \"'A'ishah (RA) used to hold the opinion that when a person performing 'umrah entered the Haram (sacred precincts of Makkah), all the restrictions that applied to a pilgrim after stoning the Jamrat al-'Aqabah were lifted for him. Thus, 'A'ishah (RA) believed that after entering the Haram, she could undo her braids and comb her hair.\"\n\nHe further narrated: \"The report I mentioned was related to us by 'Abd al-Jabbar, who said: Sufyan informed us, that Ibn Jurayj heard it from Yusuf ibn Malik, who informed him on the authority of 'A'ishah bint Talhah, that 'A'ishah (RA) had instructed her to undo her hair and wash it, saying: 'When a person performing 'umrah enters the Haram, he is in the same state as a pilgrim after stoning the Jamrat al-'Aqabah.'\"\n\nAbu Bakr (the narrator) added: \"Ash-Shafi'i said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) only commanded her to leave the actions of 'umrah, namely tawaf and sa'i, not to abandon the 'umrah itself. He commanded her to enter the state of ihram for Hajj, thus making her a Qarinah (one who combines Hajj and 'umrah without exiting the state of ihram between them).'\"\n\nHe continued: \"This is according to the view of ash-Shafi'i, similar to the action of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who entered the state of ihram for 'umrah, then said: 'I do not see any other way but this one. I bear witness that I have made Hajj obligatory along with my 'umrah,' thus combining Hajj and 'umrah before performing tawaf and sa'i for the 'umrah, making him a Qarin.\"\n\nRegarding the meaning of the Prophet's (ﷺ) statement to her: \"This is the place for the 'umrah that you were unable to perform,\" Abu Bakr (the narrator) said: \"I have explained this report in detail in my lengthy treatise on the narrations of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and the differences in their wording regarding the Farewell Pilgrimage.\"\n\n---"
